# FitTrack – Fitness Center Membership & Retention Analytics

## Capstone Project Title
**FitTrack: Fitness Center Membership & Retention Intelligence Platform**

---

## Project Idea & Brief Description

FitTrack is a full-stack MERN (MongoDB, Express.js, React, Node.js) web application designed to help fitness center administrators monitor member engagement, predict churn, and improve retention outcomes through data-driven analytics.

### The Problem
Fitness centers lose 30–50% of members within the first year, primarily because they lack real-time visibility into member behaviour, attendance patterns, and membership expiry. Manual spreadsheets and disconnected tools make it impossible to act proactively.

### The Solution
FitTrack provides a centralised analytics dashboard where admins can:
- **Track all members** — Add, view, update, and delete member records
- **Monitor attendance** — Record check-ins and view attendance trends
- **Manage memberships** — Track active plans, renewal dates, and expirations
- **Analyse retention** — View renewal rates, non-renewal rates, and engagement scores
- **Identify at-risk members** — AI-powered insights flag members likely to churn
- **Download reports** — Export analytical reports as CSV for stakeholders
- **Upload datasets** — Import bulk member data via CSV uploads

### Tech Stack
| Layer | Technology |
|-------|-----------|
| Frontend | React 18 + Vite + React Router + Axios + Lucide Icons |
| Backend | Node.js + Express.js + JWT Authentication |
| Database | MongoDB + Mongoose ODM |
| AI Feature | Gemini API — Retention Insights Assistant |
| Testing | Jest + Supertest |
| DevOps | Docker + Docker Compose + Render + Vercel |
| API Docs | Bruno Collections |

---

## Day-by-Day Capstone Development Plan

### Week 1 — Foundation & Backend

| Day | Date | Tasks |
|-----|------|-------|
| **Day 1** | Nov 18 | Set up GitHub repository · Initialise MERN project structure · Create `.gitignore` and root `package.json` · Define folder layout (`backend/`, `frontend/`, `tests/`, `bruno/`) |
| **Day 2** | Nov 19 | Design MongoDB schema — `User`, `Member`, `Membership`, `Attendance` models · Set up Express server with CORS + Morgan + dotenv · Connect MongoDB with graceful offline fallback · Create health check endpoint |
| **Day 3** | Nov 20 | Build all CRUD APIs for Members — GET all, GET by ID, POST, PUT, DELETE · Implement offline fallback store for development without MongoDB · Test all endpoints manually |
| **Day 4** | Nov 21 | Build Attendance APIs — record check-ins, view attendance history · Build Membership APIs — list plans, update status, track expiry dates · Build Analytics API — renewal rate, non-renewal rate, avg attendance, engagement score |
| **Day 5** | Nov 22 | Implement JWT Authentication — register, login, protected routes · Build admin login controller with offline fallback · Create `authMiddleware.js` to guard private routes · Add `bcryptjs` password hashing |
| **Day 6** | Nov 23 | Implement Google OAuth simulation (third-party auth) · Add CSV file upload endpoint using `multer` · Build Reports API — generate and download CSV analytical reports · Set up Bruno API collection with all endpoints documented |
| **Day 7** | Nov 24 | Write Jest + Supertest automated tests for auth, member CRUD, and analytics · Fix all failing tests · Run full backend test suite · Review and clean up all backend code |

---

### Week 2 — Frontend, AI & Deployment

| Day | Date | Tasks |
|-----|------|-------|
| **Day 8** | Nov 25 | Initialise React 18 + Vite frontend · Set up React Router for all pages · Create `AuthContext` for JWT state management · Build `ProtectedRoute` component · Configure Vite proxy to backend |
| **Day 9** | Nov 26 | Build Login page (username/password + Google OAuth button) · Build Navbar and Sidebar components · Build Dashboard page with KPI cards (total members, renewals, cancellations, avg attendance) |
| **Day 10** | Nov 27 | Build Members page — data table with Add/Edit/Delete modals · Build Attendance page — check-in recorder and history table · Build Membership page — plan cards with expiry tracking |
| **Day 11** | Nov 28 | Build Analytics page — renewal rate chart, engagement levels, at-risk member list · Build Reports page — download CSV buttons for all report types · Build CSV Upload modal for bulk data import |
| **Day 12** | Nov 29 | Integrate Gemini API for AI Retention Insights Assistant · Build `RetentionAiModal` component that analyses member stats and suggests engagement strategies · Connect all frontend pages to backend APIs via Axios service layer |
| **Day 13** | Nov 30 | Write Dockerfiles for frontend and backend · Create `docker-compose.yml` for multi-container local deployment · Test full Docker deployment locally · Set up `render.yaml` for backend cloud deployment |
| **Day 14** | Dec 1 | Deploy backend to Render.com · Deploy frontend to Vercel · Configure environment variables in cloud · Verify full-stack app runs in production · Fix any deployment issues |
| **Day 15** | Dec 2 | Final review — test all 7 pages end-to-end · Complete Bruno API documentation · Write `DEFENCE_GUIDE.md` for technical defence prep · Final commit and push · Submit project + prepare for technical defence presentation |

